================================================================================
CS744 Lab 4 - Load Test 1: Prime Number Check (CPU-bound)
================================================================================

1. AIM:
   How does throughput and mean response time change with load for a CPU-bound request under single-threaded, thread-per-request, and varying thread pool sizes?

2. SETUP & EXECUTION:
   Machine: Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11400H @ 2.70GHz (6 physical cores, 12 hyperthreads)
   Server core assignment: taskset -c 0,1 (Physical Cores 0 and 1)
   Load generator (wrk) assignment: taskset -c 2,3,4,5 (Physical Cores 2, 3, 4, 5)
   Measurement duration: 10s per point
   Varying parameter: Concurrency -c over [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128]
   Client threads: -t = min(c, 4)
   Metrics: Throughput (requests/sec) and Mean Response Time (ms)

3. HYPOTHESIS:
   For CPU-heavy work, throughput is constrained by CPU cores. Single-threaded will peak around 1 core capacity (~6k req/s). Thread pool of 1 will match single-threaded. Thread pool of 2 will double throughput (~12k req/s) by saturating both cores (CPUs 0,1). Larger thread pools (4, 8) will not increase throughput further as only 2 CPU cores are available. Thread-per-request will suffer from repeated thread creation/destruction overhead and perform similarly to or worse than single-threaded.

